## Tableau Workbook Design Guide

Here's how to build each visualization in Tableau using the exported CSVs:

### Data Connection Setup

1. **Primary Data Source:** Connect to `01_master_facility_emissions.csv`
2. **Join** with `facility_points.csv` on `facility_name` (for lat/lon if not in master)
3. **Spatial file:** Import `la_county_zipcodes.geojson` for choropleth

---

### Visualization 1: Pie/Donut Charts (Sector Share)

| Element | Tableau Config |
|---------|---------------|
| Chart Type | Pie chart (Marks card > Pie) |
| Angle | SUM(total_emissions_mtco2e) |
| Color | sector_clean |
| Filter | Create parameter for period selection (Last Year / 5yr / Decade / All) |
| Pages | Year (for animation) |

**Better alternative in Tableau:** Use a **Treemap** instead. It handles many categories more effectively and shows relative proportions clearly.

### Visualization 2: Choropleth / Heat Map

| Element | Tableau Config |
|---------|---------------|
| Map Type | Filled Map |
| Geography | Zip Code (geographic role) or join to spatial file |
| Color | SUM(total_emissions_mtco2e), color palette: Orange-Red sequential |
| Detail | facility_name (for tooltip) |
| Filter | Year, Sector |
| Pages | Year (for animated time-lapse) |

### Visualization 3: Facility Heatmap (Table)

| Element | Tableau Config |
|---------|---------------|
| Rows | facility_name (filtered to Top N) |
| Columns | year |
| Color | SUM(total_emissions_mtco2e) |
| Mark Type | Square |
