## Additional Recommended Visualizations

Beyond pie charts and choropleths, here are visualization types that work exceptionally well for this data:

| Viz Type | Best For | Why |
|----------|----------|-----|
| **Treemap** | Sector + facility hierarchy | Shows part-to-whole with drill-down (sector > company > facility) |
| **Stacked Area Chart** | Sector trends over time | Shows both total and composition change |
| **Bump Chart** | Ranking changes | Reveals which polluters are rising/falling |
| **Small Multiples** | Comparing facilities | Same chart repeated per facility for easy comparison |
| **Waterfall Chart** | Year-over-year change | Shows what added/reduced emissions between periods |
| **Diverging Bar** | Change analysis | Facilities that increased vs. decreased emissions |
| **Bubble Map** | Facility-level geography | More precise than choropleth for point sources |
| **Lollipop Chart** | Top N rankings | Cleaner than bar chart for ranked lists |

